<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the First Coalition</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1792">1792</a>–<a href="/years/1797">1797</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the First Coalition (1792–1797) was the first of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a>, fought by revolutionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and other states. After early setbacks France conquered the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Republic, and Prussia and Spain made peace in 1795. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a>'s Italian campaign forced Austria to accept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-campo-formio">Treaty of Campo Formio</a> in 1797, leaving Britain alone at war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-first-coalition.jpg" alt="War of the First Coalition" width="320" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ruedi33a · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:War_of_the_first_coalition.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
